                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3619: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-17T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:34
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>386. Japanese Minister officially informed Foreign Office that Hsu had escaped
                    from the Japanese Legation night of 14th. Unconfirmed rumors state that [he] has
                    fled to Mongolia. Another theory from Chinese sources is that Hsu is going to
                    Shanghai to intrigue with Canton, forming [Anfuite] provincial coalition against
                    Peking. Reported also Nishihara in Shanghai negotiating Japanese loan to
                    South.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
